title: 'people-westend, yet-another-parachain: add the missing parachain-system storage migrations'

doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Node Operator]
    description: |
      `cumulus-pallet-parachain-system` is at storage version 4 (#12876 changed the value type of
      `LastProcessedHrmpMessage` from `InboundMessageId` to `InboundHrmpMessageId`), but the
      People Westend and Yet Another Parachain runtimes never listed `migration::v3::Migration`
      and `migration::MigrateV3ToV4`, unlike the other Westend system chains. They now run both
      as permanent migrations. Without them, the first runtime upgrade of such a chain leaves the
      pallet at its old storage version and `LastProcessedHrmpMessage` in the old encoding, which
      the new code cannot decode: reads of it log `Corrupted state` and fall back to a default
      until a block that processes inbound HRMP messages overwrites it, and `try-runtime` rejects
      the upgrade on the storage-version mismatch. Both migrations are no-ops once the on-chain
      version is current.

crates:
  - name: people-westend-runtime
    bump: patch
  - name: yet-another-parachain-runtime
    bump: patch
